{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And he shall split.</b> שִׁסּוּעַ is only by hand, and so it says of Samson: ״וַיְשַׁסְּעֵהוּ כְּשַׁסַּע הַגְּדִי״ (Judges 14)." "<b>With its wings.</b> Together with its wings — he need not pluck its feathered wings." "<b>With its wings.</b> Actual plumage. And is there any ordinary person who smells the odor of burnt wings and is not nauseated by it? Why then does Scripture say 'he shall offer'? So that the altar be sated and adorned with the offering of the poor (Leviticus Rabbah 3)." "<b>He shall not divide it.</b> He does not sever it completely into two pieces, but tears it from the back. 'A pleasing odor' is said of a bird and 'a pleasing odor' is said of an animal — to tell you: whether one gives much or one gives little, so long as he directs his heart to heaven (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:42.243345586Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}